1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,760
[ZH] 在那時候,我遇到千萬人

2
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:08,200
[ZH] 他們從不同的背景、不同的教育、生活方式

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:13,480
[ZH] 一些因為他們感到疾瘋,其他人在疾瘋

4
00:00:13,480 --> 00:00:18,680
[ZH] 其他人在結婚,其他人想變得更好的父母、更好的主持人

5
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:21,600
[ZH] 或是更好的自己的版本

6
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:25,720
[ZH] 在過去的二十年裡面,我擔任心理健康治療師

7
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:44,920
[ZH] 那在這段指甲裡面,我接觸過上千位的個案,他們都是不同的原因來找我的,可能是焦慮,可能是哀傷,可能是婚姻出了一些狀況,或是希望成為更好的父母,或是優秀的領導者,或是單純想成為更好的指甲。

8
00:00:44,920 --> 00:01:05,400
[ZH] 雖然每個人都帶著不同的生命故事來找我,可是卻有一個問題反復出現,心理治療真的對我有幫助嗎?

9
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:26,500
[ZH] 那這個問題呢 我寫下了一本書 書名就叫做 心理治療 它是改變人生的契機 還是一種生活型態 還是根本就浪費時間

10
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:33,300
[ZH] 現在是一種誤會的題目,因為在我的經歷,所有三個答案都可以正確。

11
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:33,360
[EN]  can be true.

12
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:38,340
[EN]  For some people, therapy changes the course of their lives, but for others, therapy becomes

13
00:01:38,340 --> 00:01:44,600
[EN]  a weekly habit without producing meaningful change, and unfortunately, some people spend

14
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:50,020
[EN]  months or even years in therapy, and walk away disappointed, wondering why nothing ever

15
00:01:50,020 --> 00:01:51,020
[EN]  changed.

16
00:01:51,020 --> 00:01:57,880
[EN]  Now today, I'd like to answer a different question, how do you get the most out of therapy?

17
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:27,480
[ZH] 還有對一群人來說,有些人花了很多很多的時間進行心理治療,可是最後卻什麼都沒有改變

18
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:29,480
[ZH] 所以這三種狀況都是有可能會發生的

19
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:37,480
[ZH] 那我今天想要問你一個問題是,你如何要從心理治療獲得最大的注意?就是我今天的講題

20
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:42,480
[ZH] 所以不單止是否有醫療效果,但是否有醫療效果

21
00:02:42,480 --> 00:02:46,480
[ZH] 是一番重要的事情在臺灣。

22
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:50,480
[ZH] 健康健康健康的社會是越來越多。

23
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:52,480
[ZH] 那是最新的。

24
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:54,480
[ZH] 有關的病毒是在增加的病毒。

25
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:57,480
[ZH] 更多人會願意請求救助。

26
00:02:57,480 --> 00:03:00,480
[ZH] 但在同時,很多人都不在乎。

27
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:02,480
[ZH] 什麼事情在病毒?

28
00:03:02,480 --> 00:03:04,480
[ZH] 誰要去?

29
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:06,480
[ZH] 我需要去?

30
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:08,480
[ZH] 我需要我去做朋友嗎?

31
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:10,480
[ZH] 我需要知道我的朋友嗎?

32
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:25,460
[ZH] 那我相信就是心理治療要怎麼樣獲得助力在臺灣也是一個很重要的議題

33
00:03:25,460 --> 00:03:28,240
[ZH] 因為其實全世界現在都很重視心理健康

34
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:32,400
[ZH] 那越來越多人是主動願意去做心理治療的

35
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:37,640
[ZH] 但是還是很多人在做心理治療的同時大家會心中有疑問

36
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:58,600
[ZH] 心理治療的過程中到底有幫助是,誰真正需要做心理治療,尋求心理治療是不是代表我是一個很弱的人,或是說我不要心理治療是不是也可以找朋友聊聊就好了,或是說我如何知道心理師真的對我有幫助,那這些都是很好的問題,那我希望今天演講結束的時候大家的這些問題都可以獲得解答。

37
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:01,060
[ZH] 今天我不是要去認識每個人都應該在認識

38
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:04,400
[ZH] 在認識,我認為一些人不需要認識

39
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:07,380
[ZH] 一些人只需要一個友調的朋友

40
00:04:07,380 --> 00:04:09,520
[ZH] 一些人只需要更多睡

41
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:11,140
[ZH] 或健康的 habits

42
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:12,440
[ZH] 或更多健康

43
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:14,720
[ZH] 一些人需要 difficult conversations

44
00:04:14,720 --> 00:04:16,400
[ZH] 一些人只需要 slow down

45
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:20,840
[ZH] 認識是一種重要的東西

46
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:22,240
[ZH] 它不是唯一的東西

47
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:27,200
[ZH] 而解識的方法和方法是一種重要的東西

48
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:30,400
[ZH] 請大家不要以為我今天是來宣傳

49
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:32,300
[ZH] 每個人都應該去做心理治療

50
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:34,600
[ZH] 事實上我相信很多人是不需要的

51
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:38,800
[ZH] 有些人其實只是需要一位可以彈心的好朋友

52
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:40,500
[ZH] 或是更衝突的睡眠

53
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:42,400
[ZH] 或是更健康的生活習慣

54
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:47,000
[ZH] 或是隻是需要鼓起勇氣來進行一次困難的對話

55
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
[ZH] 有些人只是要讓生活慢下來

56
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,600
[ZH] 所以心理治療是一個工具

57
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:52,500
[ZH] 但它並不是唯一的工具

58
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:54,300
[ZH] 明白什麼時候該使用它

59
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:57,000
[ZH] 如何善用它才是最重要的

60
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:00,140
[ZH]  Now, one of my favorite experiences happened when I was in graduate school.

61
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:09,120
[EN]  One of my professors was a renowned psychologist who specialised in treating military veterans suffering from post-traumatic stress disorder.

62
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:19,200
[EN]  For 12 weeks, we studied his methods. He explained diagnostic criteria, he discussed treatment models, he taught us sophisticated therapeutic techniques.

63
00:05:19,780 --> 00:05:28,820
[EN]  then finally came the day i'd been waiting for we watched videos of his actual therapy sessions

64
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:35,940
[EN]  and i was excited i thought i was about to watch a master perform something extraordinary

65
00:05:36,820 --> 00:05:45,700
[EN]  i expected psychological brilliance instead he greeted the client warmly he asked one question

66
00:05:46,740 --> 00:05:54,500
[EN]  tell me about your week. Then he barely bloody said a word. The client talked, and the professor

67
00:05:54,500 --> 00:06:00,100
[EN]  listened. The client talked more, and the professor nodded. Occasionally he asked a thoughtful

68
00:06:22,460 --> 00:06:25,460
[ZH] 然後有一天我們在課堂上要看老師示範

69
00:06:25,460 --> 00:06:28,460
[ZH] 就是他是如何進行心理治療的錄影帶

70
00:06:28,460 --> 00:06:31,460
[ZH] 那我就很興奮想說我要看到大師出馬了

71
00:06:31,460 --> 00:06:34,460
[ZH] 然後在影片裡面我只看到我的教授

72
00:06:34,460 --> 00:06:36,460
[ZH] 就是很溫暖的跟個案問個好

73
00:06:36,460 --> 00:06:39,460
[ZH] 然後呢就說你跟我說說你這一週過得如何

74
00:06:39,460 --> 00:06:41,460
[ZH] 然後接下來我的教授就不怎麼講話

75
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:43,460
[ZH] 就是隻有個案一直講

76
00:06:43,460 --> 00:06:45,460
[ZH] 然後教授專注聽

77
00:06:45,460 --> 00:06:48,460
[ZH] 然後呢偶爾教授會提出一個很好的問題

78
00:06:48,460 --> 00:06:49,460
[ZH] 但是主要就是個案在講

79
00:06:49,460 --> 00:06:51,460
[ZH] 然後就這樣結束了

80
00:06:52,460 --> 00:06:57,460
[ZH] I remember leaving the class disappointed and I thought, is that it?

81
00:06:57,460 --> 00:07:00,460
[ZH] The client did most of the talking.

82
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:04,720
[EN]  Now, as a young student, I completely misunderstood what I'd just witnessed.

83
00:07:05,780 --> 00:07:12,460
[EN]  Today, after two decades as a therapist, I realized I had actually watched a master at work.

84
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:15,820
[EN]  He understood something that many people misunderstand.

85
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:19,320
[EN]  The therapist was never supposed to be the hero.

86
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:20,660
[EN]  The client was.

87
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:23,900
[EN]  The therapist was not there to rescue someone.

88
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:29,300
[EN]  who has created a safe environment where another human being could discover truth,

89
00:07:29,300 --> 00:07:33,300
[EN]  develop insight, and begin changing his own life.

90
00:07:33,260 --> 00:07:37,960
[ZH] That lesson changed the way I understand therapy.

91
00:07:51,460 --> 00:08:14,260
[ZH] 他示範了,在心靈治療裡面,治療師從來就不應該是那個主角,個案自己才是,所以我們的治療師不是要前來拯救誰,我們的職責是要創造一個安全的空間,然後讓一個生命可以在這個安全的空間裡面發現真相,然後能親自改變自己的人生。

92
00:08:19,980 --> 00:08:46,080
[EN*]  We don't fortune tell. We don't man-read. We're not professional advice givers. Good therapists certainly have knowledge. They understand psychology, human behaviour. They understand research. But their greatest skill is often much simpler. They know how to listen. They know how to ask the right questions. They know how to help people see what they've been able to see on their own.

93
00:08:46,640 --> 00:08:53,640
[EN*]  This is very different from solving someone's problems. In fact, I haven't told people this

94
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:34,720
[EN*]  This is what I tell people, the goal of therapy is not to make you dependent on your therapist.

95
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:41,760
[EN]  The goal of therapy is to make you increasingly capable without your therapist.

96
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:46,160
[EN]  That single sentence captures almost everything I believe about the therapy.

97
00:09:46,160 --> 00:09:48,820
[EN]  Therapy should increase your capacity.

98
00:09:49,420 --> 00:09:56,300
[EN]  Your capacity to think, to regulate emotions, to solve problems, to build healthy relationships.

99
00:09:57,440 --> 00:10:00,640
[EN]  Your capacity to face suffering without becoming overwhelmed.

100
00:10:04,420 --> 00:10:12,220
[ZH] 它會成為一名的最大的投資,但這提起另一個重要的問題,

101
00:10:12,220 --> 00:10:16,420
[ZH] 如果療療有那麼多的能力,為什麼有些人感受驚喜的變化,

102
00:10:16,420 --> 00:10:20,420
[ZH] 而其他人感受驚喜幾乎沒有?

103
00:10:20,420 --> 00:10:24,420
[ZH] 事實上,我常常會講這句話,心理治療的目標,

104
00:10:24,420 --> 00:10:26,980
[ZH] 不是讓你依賴你的治療師

105
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:29,780
[ZH] 他的目標是讓你即使沒有治療師

106
00:10:29,780 --> 00:10:33,780
[ZH] 也可以越來越具備自主面對人生的能力

107
00:10:33,780 --> 00:10:39,380
[ZH] 那這句話就概括了我對於優質心理治療的這個信念

108
00:10:39,380 --> 00:10:44,420
[ZH] 一個好的心理治療應該可以拓展你的生命的能力

109
00:10:44,420 --> 00:10:47,140
[ZH] 包含你怎麼樣去調節情緒

110
00:10:47,140 --> 00:10:49,060
[ZH] 怎麼樣去解決問題

111
00:10:49,060 --> 00:10:51,540
[ZH] 怎麼樣去建立健康人際關係

112
00:10:51,540 --> 00:10:55,620
[ZH] 還有讓你面對人生苦難不至於被打倒

113
00:10:55,620 --> 00:10:58,620
[ZH] 壓垮的一個心理容量

114
00:10:58,620 --> 00:11:01,420
[ZH] 所以當如果你的心理治療可以達到這些目標的話

115
00:11:01,420 --> 00:11:04,060
[ZH] 它就是一個很值得的自我投資

116
00:11:04,060 --> 00:11:06,580
[ZH] 但是這個引出了另外一個重要的問題

117
00:11:06,580 --> 00:11:08,120
[ZH] 就是為什麼心理治療

118
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:10,160
[ZH] 假設說有這麼大的好處的話

119
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:14,060
[ZH] 為什麼有些人做心理治療以後可以有驚人的蛻變

120
00:11:14,060 --> 00:11:16,940
[ZH] 但是有些人卻沒有什麼進展

121
00:11:16,940 --> 00:11:21,940
[ZH] 現在二十多年醫療工作後,我來到一個簡單的結論。

122
00:11:21,940 --> 00:11:27,940
[ZH] 差別是不少智慧,不少教育,也不少是有一個重點。

123
00:11:27,940 --> 00:11:32,940
[ZH] 最大的差別是這個。

124
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:44,160
[EN*]  經過十年的臨床的經驗,我得出了一個結論,有些人會覺得很有幫助,有些人會覺得沒有變化,關鍵在於這句話。

125
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:48,160
[EN*]  Are you ready? Drum roll.

126
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:58,160
[EN*]  The people who benefit most understand that therapy is not something that is done to them, it is something they actively participate in.

127
00:11:58,160 --> 00:12:04,520
[EN*]  in. The client is not a passenger, the client is a partner. And that brings up the central

128
00:12:04,520 --> 00:12:08,780
[EN]  idea I want to leave with you today. Therapy is not magic. Therapists are not magicians.

129
00:12:09,440 --> 00:12:13,400
[EN]  Real change happens when an effective therapist and a committed client work together towards

130
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:19,400
[EN]  the same goal. When both bring what they are supposed to bring, therapy can truly become

131
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:32,400
[EN]  The question then is simple. What does the client need to bring? That is what I'd like to spend the rest of our time exploring together.

132
00:12:36,080 --> 00:12:43,480
[ZH] 心理治療並不是由外強加在他們身上的事情

133
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:47,400
[ZH] 而是需要按住自己全新投入主動參與的歷程

134
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:50,760
[ZH] 也就是說個案並不應該是一個被動的被施加者

135
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:52,840
[ZH] 而是一個平等的作夥伴

136
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:56,100
[ZH] 所以真正的好的改變會發生在於

137
00:12:56,100 --> 00:13:00,240
[ZH] 個案跟治療師攜手有一個共同的目標一起努力

138
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:03,800
[ZH] 這樣才可以發揮心理治療的力量

139
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:11,800
[ZH] 所以,客戶是甚麼帶來的? 後來年長的工作,年輕人,年輕人,婚姻,家庭,我發現了甚麼。

140
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:22,800
[ZH] 人們所感到的最大的改變,不是最大的最大人,最貴重,最貴重的問題,他們是人們所面對的改善療程度。

141
00:13:22,800 --> 00:13:29,800
[ZH] 今天,我希望分享五個技術,我相信會幫助人們最大的改善療程度。

142
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:39,800
[ZH] 那假設今天大家的身份是來做心理治療的個案,那身為個案你需要為你的治療帶來什麼?你才可以讓心理治療對你發出最大的注意。

143
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:49,200
[EN*]  One, come with a purpose.

144
00:13:49,200 --> 00:14:12,840
[EN*]  One of the first questions I ask a new client is surprisingly simple. What would you like to be different? Sometimes the answer comes quickly. I want to stop having panic attacks. I want to save a marriage. I want to stop yelling at my children. I want to feel confident. But many people don't know. They simply say, I don't know. I just know I don't want to feel like this anymore.

145
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:17,240
[EN*]  That's what I'm asking for.

146
00:14:17,240 --> 00:14:21,240
[EN*]  The first question is that you need a very clear purpose to do that.

147
00:14:21,240 --> 00:14:26,240
[EN*]  The first question is that you hope your life will change your life.

148
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:29,240
[EN*]  Some people can tell you a very specific answer.

149
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:32,240
[EN*]  For example, I want to find out my marriage.

150
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:34,240
[EN*]  But many people don't have answers.

151
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:37,240
[EN*]  They say I don't know. I just don't want to cry.

152
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:40,240
[EN*]  At the beginning, no answer is fine.

153
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:50,740
[EN*]  that's perfectly okay sometimes therapy begins with confusion but

154
00:14:50,740 --> 00:14:55,720
[EN*]  eventually confusion becomes clarity now imagine you hide the taxi driver you

155
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:59,020
[EN*]  climb into the back seat and the driver turns around and asks where'd you like

156
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:04,000
[EN*]  to go and you answer I don't know how can the driver possibly get you there

157
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:09,100
[EN*]  therapy works the same way a therapist cannot help you move toward a destination

158
00:15:09,100 --> 00:15:25,740
[EN*]  that neither of you can describe. Notice I didn't say you need to know exactly how you'll get there, that's the therapist's job, but you should eventually know where you're trying to go. In my book, I distinguish between two broad purposes for therapy.

159
00:15:43,900 --> 00:15:52,180
[ZH] 可是你至少要提供一個你想要前往的方向,那在我的書裡面,我將治療的目的分成兩個型別。

160
00:15:52,180 --> 00:16:16,180
[ZH] 第一次是我稱為是emote therapy,這是一個生意的方法,讓你感受到的感受,有很大的價值,很多人持有負責,他們沒有說謊,他們花了一年在扮演,全部都好,醫生給他們讓他們讓他們扮演,有時那一刻是深刻的癒癒。

161
00:16:16,180 --> 00:16:24,640
[ZH] 那第一個型別就是讓我的案主有一個情緒宣洩和安全感的一個空間

162
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:29,700
