223
00:22:58,340 --> 00:23:04,340
[EN*]  But learning only becomes change when those skills leaves the therapist's office and enter ordinary life.

224
00:23:04,340 --> 00:23:08,340
[EN*]  The office is the classroom, life is the examination.

225
00:23:08,340 --> 00:23:35,340
[EN*]  This is my favorite one, principle four, expect discomfort, there's no growth in the comfort zone, there's no comfort in the growth zone.

226
00:23:35,340 --> 00:24:04,200
[EN]  This principle surprises people. Good therapy often feels uncomfortable. Growth usually does. Think about physical exercise. If you never increase resistance, your muscle never becomes stronger. Our emotional lives work pretty much the same way. Many people begin therapy hoping difficult emotions will disappear. Instead, they sometimes discover those emotions become more noticeable for a while. Why? Because they finally stop running from them.

227
00:24:18,620 --> 00:24:23,460
[ZH] 如果你不增加那個重量,阻力的話,你就沒有辦法變得更強壯

