231
00:24:54,340 --> 00:25:01,340
[EN*]  I frequently remind clients, if I don't challenge you, it probably won't change you.

232
00:25:01,300 --> 00:25:04,940
[ZH]  temporary discomfort is often the price of long term freedom

233
00:25:04,940 --> 00:25:11,200
[ZH] 那有的時候要獲得療癒就是必須要重新面對一些不想面對的記憶

234
00:25:11,200 --> 00:25:13,520
[ZH] 或是進行一些很困難的對話

235
00:25:13,520 --> 00:25:16,140
[ZH] 或是要去勇於面對自己的責任

236
00:25:16,140 --> 00:25:21,360
[ZH] 甚至要去原諒一些其實現實中都沒有向你道歉的人在心裡原諒他們

237
00:25:21,360 --> 00:25:23,500
[ZH] 那我會跟我的客戶說

238
00:25:23,500 --> 00:25:27,540
[ZH] 如果這件事情沒有為你帶來挑戰的感覺

239
00:25:27,540 --> 00:25:30,240
[ZH] 那他大概也很難為你帶來改變

240
00:25:43,780 --> 00:25:51,840
[EN]  Too many people attend therapy for months or are ever asking whether anything is changing. Imagine taking medication without checking whether your symptoms improved.

241
00:25:52,360 --> 00:25:57,140
[EN]  Or taking piano lessons without noticing whether you play better, progress matters.

242
00:25:57,500 --> 00:26:02,340
