280
00:29:26,660 --> 00:29:30,880
[EN]  Trust does not always develop in one session. Sometimes it does take time.

281
00:29:40,800 --> 00:30:08,940
[EN*]  but without trust, therapy becomes very difficult. I remember training him a therapist though in his career. One day he came to me excited. He said, my client finally trusts me. He was celebrating because that's taken several weeks and I smiled and congratulated him.

282
00:30:08,940 --> 00:30:14,660
[EN*]  Then I said something he's never forgotten. I said, good, now you can really finally start the work.

283
00:30:15,200 --> 00:30:20,080
[EN*]  And he looked surprised. He thought, I didn't trust to be the destination. It wasn't. It was just a doorway.

284
00:30:21,900 --> 00:30:26,500
[EN*]  Trust is essential, but trust is never the finish line. It is the beginning of the work.

285
00:30:38,940 --> 00:30:55,000
[EN*]  Question two, does my therapist have a clear process?

286
00:30:55,000 --> 00:31:00,900
[EN*]  Now imagine visiting a physician, you describe your symptoms, your doctor listens carefully,

287
00:31:00,900 --> 00:31:07,100
[EN]  then says, I'm not really sure what we're going to do, let's just keep talking every week and see what happens.

288
00:31:07,100 --> 00:31:13,120
[EN]  Well, most of us would probably seek a second opinion, yet this sometimes happens in therapy.

289
00:31:13,720 --> 00:31:16,160
[EN]  Good therapists may use different methods.

290
00:31:16,600 --> 00:31:20,320
[EN]  Some use cognitive behavioural therapy, others use acceptance and commitment therapy.

291
00:31:21,060 --> 00:31:28,040
[EN]  Often others use solution-focused therapy, others integrate several research-based approaches.

292
00:31:28,660 --> 00:31:33,200
[EN]  The exact model matters less than many people think.

293
00:31:33,200 --> 00:31:37,000
[EN*]  What matters is that your therapist has a thoughtful framework.

294
00:31:37,100 --> 00:32:04,620
[EN*]  Now, there should be tension behind what happens during your session.

295
00:32:04,620 --> 00:32:12,960
[EN*]  The therapist should know why they're asking these questions, why they're teaching particular skills, and why they believe this approach fits our situation.

296
00:32:13,840 --> 00:32:18,960
[EN*]  You deserve more than pleasant conversations. You deserve purposeful conversations.

297
00:32:34,620 --> 00:32:43,660
[EN*]  last question question three am i changing this may be the most important question of all

298
00:32:43,660 --> 00:32:48,580
[EN*]  sometimes people stay in therapy for years without stopping to ask whether their lives

299
00:32:48,580 --> 00:32:54,740
[EN*]  are actually improving now please don't misunderstand me healing is really quick

300
00:32:54,740 --> 00:33:01,680
[EN*]  growth is rarely linear some weeks will feel discouraging some weeks may even feel worse

301
00:33:02,800 --> 00:33:04,800
[ZH] and feel better

302
00:33:04,800 --> 00:33:05,800
[ZH] and that's normal

303
00:33:05,800 --> 00:33:24,800
[ZH] 第三個可以問的問題是我是否有在發生改變,因為治療並不是一個線性前進的歷程,有時候會比較慢,有時候會有上下起起伏伏,可是你應該是可以看到有一些推進的。

304
00:33:24,800 --> 00:33:51,800
[ZH] 但在時間上,你應該知道它的動作。可能你會回復後面的緊急,可能你的心情沒有控制每個決定。可能你會更正確的。可能你的家人會發現你會更加悲慘。可能你會睡得更好。可能你會比較多。可能你會比較多刺激。這些改變可能會變小,但你永遠不會再過測低小的改變,再繼續繼續。

305
00:33:54,800 --> 00:33:59,200
[ZH] 有一些推進,比如說衝突以後是不是可以更快的復原

306
00:33:59,200 --> 00:34:03,700
[ZH] 那焦慮不再主宰你的決定,你是不是可以更坦誠的溝通

307
00:34:22,180 --> 00:34:28,680
[EN*]  himself during the day. That was it. Nothing complicated, just a tally. To his surprise,

308
00:34:29,140 --> 00:34:33,460
[EN*]  after only a few weeks, those numbers began dropping. Why? Because paying attention created

309
00:34:31,600 --> 00:34:34,600
[ZH] 為什麼?因為要注意力,令人變得更多。

310
00:34:34,600 --> 00:34:36,600
[ZH] 因為要注意力,令人變得更多。

311
00:34:36,600 --> 00:34:40,600
[ZH] 所以,要注意力,令人變得更多。

312
00:34:40,600 --> 00:34:42,600
[ZH] 所以,要問問你,

313
00:34:42,600 --> 00:34:45,600
[ZH] 什麼是今天,對六個月後?

314
00:34:45,600 --> 00:34:47,600
[ZH] 如果答案是沒有,

315
00:34:47,600 --> 00:34:50,600
[ZH] 便是時間,要談談談談談。

316
00:34:50,600 --> 00:35:20,580
[ZH] 那像我有一次有一個客戶,她就是,她的目標是要減少她批評自己的時間和次數,所以她就開始算,她每天都花時間自我批評,那後來幾個禮拜過後她發現這個數字有在下降,所以就告訴我們說,其實有的時候改變是起於就是你有意識到我們要做某件事情,那意識就會帶來改變,所以就是請持續的問自己說,我今天很想要去做什麼事情,我們要去做什麼事情,我們要去做什麼事情。

317
00:35:20,580 --> 00:35:29,040
[ZH] 如果六個月前有什麼不一樣,那如果沒有什麼不一樣的話,那可能就是跟你的治療師要再溝通討論。

318
00:35:29,040 --> 00:35:33,360
[ZH] 而我們繼續今天 我 would like to leave you with this one

319
00:35:39,080 --> 00:35:44,460
[EN]  Wisdom is more than knowledge. Wisdom is learning how to live well.

320
00:35:45,260 --> 00:35:51,020
[EN]  I believe therapy, at its very best, is one pathway toward that wisdom.

321
00:35:52,020 --> 00:35:54,600
[EN]  It helps us understand ourselves more honestly.

322
00:35:55,520 --> 00:35:58,260
[EN]  It teaches us healthier ways to respond to suffering.

323
00:35:59,000 --> 00:36:00,960
[EN]  It strengthens our relationships.

324
00:36:01,340 --> 00:36:04,340
[EN]  It replaces unhealthy habits with healthier ones.

325
00:36:05,160 --> 00:36:13,100
[EN]  Perhaps most importantly, it reminds us that while we cannot always control what happens to us, we can always control how we respond.

326
00:36:14,260 --> 00:36:21,200
[EN]  Life will bring disappointment, stress, loss, failure, conflict. No one escapes these experiences.

327
00:36:22,080 --> 00:36:28,820
[EN]  The question is not whether life will be difficult. The question is whether we will develop the skills to meet those difficulties well.

328
00:36:29,640 --> 00:36:32,280
[EN]  That is where therapy can make an extraordinary difference.

329
00:36:47,180 --> 00:36:54,380
[ZH] 教導我們怎麼樣健康地面對挫敗 還有苦難 還有深化我們的人際關係

330
00:36:54,380 --> 00:36:59,220
[ZH] 然後提醒我們雖然我們沒有辦法永遠掌握外在發生在我們的事

331
00:36:59,220 --> 00:37:04,780
[ZH] 可是我們可以學習如何選擇自己回應這些事情的方式

332
00:37:04,780 --> 00:37:08,020
[ZH] 所以生命一定會有起起伏伏

333
00:37:08,020 --> 00:37:12,180
[ZH] 那關鍵不是在於我們會不會遇到這些磨難

334
00:37:12,180 --> 00:37:16,180
[ZH] 而是我們有沒有具備因應這些挑戰的適應技巧

335
00:37:16,180 --> 00:37:27,600
[ZH] 我開始寫這個詞,我問了一個詞,是否有生命的一切?是否有生命?是否有生命?或是否有空間?

336
00:37:27,600 --> 00:37:37,480
[ZH] 然後,20年來的一切,我相信是十分之一樣的答案,是否有生命的一切。人們的一切。

337
00:37:33,500 --> 00:37:36,460
[EN]  Therapy by itself doesn't change lives.

338
00:37:37,020 --> 00:37:37,480
[EN]  People do.

339
00:37:38,300 --> 00:37:43,900
[EN]  Therapy simply gives people the knowledge, the skills, and the opportunity to change.

340
00:37:44,600 --> 00:37:48,300
[EN]  But the decision to change, that always belongs to the individual.

341
00:37:49,600 --> 00:37:55,280
[EN]  If you ever decide to be in therapy, don't ask the first question that most people ask.

342
00:37:55,760 --> 00:37:58,400
[EN]  Don't ask, will therapy help me?

343
00:37:58,760 --> 00:38:21,120
[EN]  Instead, ask yourself a better question. Am I willing to become the kind of person who gets the most out of therapy? Because the greatest predictor of success is not finding the perfect therapist, it's not becoming an engaged, honest, courageous client. Sorry, it is becoming an engaged, honest, courageous client.

344
00:38:21,120 --> 00:38:28,360
[EN]  When a skilled therapist brings knowledge, and a courageous client brings commitment, transformation becomes possible.

345
00:38:29,160 --> 00:38:34,320
[EN]  I'd like to leave you with one sentence that summarizes everything I've learned from the past two decades.

346
00:38:34,980 --> 00:38:38,720
[EN]  The goal of therapy is not to be dependent on your therapist.

347
00:38:39,480 --> 00:38:44,500
[EN]  The goal of therapy is to become increasingly capable without one.

348
00:38:44,760 --> 00:38:47,380
[EN]  When therapy helps you think more clearly,

349
00:38:47,380 --> 00:38:51,020
[EN]  look more deeply, respond more wisely,

350
00:38:51,020 --> 00:38:55,220
[EN]  look more intentionally, then therapy has done its job.

351
00:38:55,220 --> 00:38:58,060
[EN]  Thank you for allowing me to share this time with you.

352
00:38:58,060 --> 00:39:00,140
[EN]  It's been an honor to be with you.

353
00:39:00,260 --> 00:39:10,260
[ZH] 我希望你 家庭和人們 為你影響的生命 為了聖誕 穩定 希望 和勇敢繼續墓 謝謝

354
00:39:30,260 --> 00:39:32,320
[ZH] 心理治療能不能幫助我

355
00:39:32,320 --> 00:39:33,620
[ZH] 而是問自己

356
00:39:33,620 --> 00:39:39,200
[ZH] 我願意成為那個從治療中獲得最大注意的主動參與者嗎

357
00:39:39,200 --> 00:39:41,660
[ZH] 那最後總結今天的分享

358
00:39:41,660 --> 00:39:44,700
[ZH] 就是心理治療目標不是讓你依賴你的治療師

359
00:39:44,700 --> 00:39:47,100
[ZH] 而是讓你在沒有治療師的時候

360
00:39:47,100 --> 00:39:49,600
[ZH] 也具有這個能力可以過得很好

361
00:39:49,600 --> 00:39:51,060
[ZH] 活出人生的精彩

362
00:39:51,060 --> 00:39:53,180
[ZH] 那祝福各位 謝謝大家

